title "From gene to trait"
layout layered dir=down
page a3
font 8pt..34pt wrap=16em

style information color=#1565C0
style process color=#2E7D32
style outcome color=#6A1B9A

node dna "DNA sequence" .information
| stored hereditary information
| double helix; complementary base pairing
node chromosome "Chromosome" .information
| DNA packaged with proteins
| homologs carry corresponding loci
node gene "Gene" .information
| functional region of DNA
| alleles are alternative sequence versions
node regulation "Gene regulation" .process
| enhancers, promoters, and transcription factors
| determines when and where a gene is used
node transcription "Transcription" .process
| DNA -> messenger RNA
| RNA polymerase reads one template strand
node mrna "mRNA" .information
| exported coding message
| introns removed; exons joined in eukaryotes
node translation "Translation" .process
| ribosome reads codons
| AUG starts; stop codons terminate
node protein "Protein" .outcome
| amino-acid chain folds into a structure
| sequence, environment, and chaperones matter
node function "Cellular function" .outcome
| catalysis, transport, signaling, or structure
| proteins interact in networks
node trait "Observable trait" .outcome
| phenotype depends on genes and environment
| one gene can affect many traits
node mutation "Mutation" .information
| sequence change created by copying or damage
| effects range from neutral to harmful or beneficial
node inheritance "Inheritance" .information
| meiosis separates alleles into gametes
| segregation predicts genotype frequencies
node variation "Population variation" .outcome
| selection, drift, migration, and mutation change frequencies
| evolution acts on heritable variation
node environment "Environment" .outcome
| nutrition, temperature, and signals alter expression
| phenotype is not genotype alone

dna -> gene
gene -> chromosome
gene -> regulation
gene -> transcription
transcription -> mrna
mrna -> translation
translation -> protein
protein -> function
function -> trait
gene -> mutation
mutation -> variation
gene -> inheritance
inheritance -> variation
environment -> regulation
environment -> trait
variation ..> trait "allele effects"

require dna at top
require trait at bottom
prefer protein near function within=14em weight=2
prefer environment near trait within=18em weight=2
